WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.690
Christian Era 2619

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:09.020
There are truly numerous things 
that can make people ill.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.470
Microbes such as bacteria and viruses...

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.450
Not to mention, there's also...

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.450
love.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.450
As I was saying,

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.360
there are bacteria that 
want to find comfortable homes

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.040
within other host organisms,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.770
but they are themselves organisms, 
so they can move, split,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.380
and multiply on their own.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.650
However, viruses do not have the 
ability to regenerate by themselves,

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:40.180
so they must live off their host to breed.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.920
They use the host's cells
in the breeding process,

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.560
and often they destroy those cells.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.050
There are also

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.190
cases where viruses from other 
animals suddenly mutate so

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.070
they can infect humans, as well...

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.270
In those cases, the virus can end 
up destroying the human cells

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.860
which they aren't accustomed to.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.780
Conversely, the human host's immune response

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.050
may overreact resulting

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.820
in failure of the host's bodily functions.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.520
This is precisely how the 
mechanism of contagious diseases

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.720
works in humans.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.610
Now, for the matter at hand...

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.470
This is the Alien Engine Virus.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:51.100
It is a new form of virus that 
we fear is starting to spread.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.280
The mortality rate for 
those infected is 100%,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.760
and its existence

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.390
has not yet been made public.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.140
Usually, even if there is a 
new strain of a virus,

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.630
there should be flora and 
fauna that contain said virus.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:15.280
However, that is not the case 
with the Alien Engine Virus.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.790
I see...

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:21.790
Moving on.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.860
It appeared suddenly forty-two years ago,

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.700
and has increased drastically 
in the last twenty years.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.290
Which means...

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.920
It's all the Captain's fault.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.170
Shut your mouth, you Russian geezer.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.900
Aw, I just got yelled at by a girl

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.050
who's about the same age as my daughter.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.210
This old man is in shock.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.510
Please listen carefully.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.990
Since we can't cultivate this virus,

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.940
in order to create a vaccine for it,

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.070
we need to obtain numerous 
samples from its source.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.030
That is why we are sending them to Mars...

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.010
For the sake of humanity's survival.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.150
Christian Era 2620

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.150
Men, this is your captain, Komachi, speaking.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.610
This vessel, Annex 1, 
has exited Earth's atmosphere

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.150
and is heading to Mars on autopilot.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.150
Until we land on Mars in thirty-nine 
days, we will have you

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.910
live in the residential quarters.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.020
<i>There is low artificial gravity 
throughout the vessel,</i>

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.430
<i>but daily training is essential in order
 to ensure your bodies don't weaken.</i>

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.590
Hey, there's gravity!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.510
I wonder how they're doing it.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:30.240
<i>As a general rule the executive 
staff area is off-limits,</i>

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.430
<i>but if there's something troubling you, 
please feel free to let me know.</i>

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.680
It's so stuffy.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:40.820
<i>By the way, out of the executives, 
Michelle and Joseph are single...</i>

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.960
<i>As well as me! So don't hesitate, all right?</i>

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.070
Talk about a captain with no sense of urgency.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.700
Yeah, seriously.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.490
Especially considering we're going to 
be risking our lives on this mission.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:02.210
Why don't you stop holding back 
and go exploring already?

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.310
Thanks!

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.310
Me first!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.770
What should we do, Kana-chan?

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.680
Why don't we find some hot guys?

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:12.810
Hey, Sheila-chan...

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.930
Could it be...

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.380
that you like the Captain?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.970
I knew it.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.670
The day before the surgery,

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.070
I was so nervous...

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.280
I got depressed, and skipped out on training.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.350
Did you

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.010
come here to take me back?

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.010
No.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.010
I came here to cry, too.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:59.100
When I want to cry, I always come 
here and cry and cry and cry,

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.690
and take my frustration 
out on the things around here.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:06.330
Otherwise, I wouldn't be able to do this.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:16.360
You're not going to tell him how you feel?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.030
O-Of course not!

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.260
There's no way the Captain 
and I would be compatible.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.480
Not to mention he's twice your age.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.170
That doesn't matter!

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.410
Um... I-I didn't...

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.430
Oh, the shower room!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.100
Let's go look at the shower room!

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:46.570
Oh. S-Sorry! We didn't know you were in here!

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:51.320
No, I'm sorry. 
Apparently I forgot to lock the door.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.840
Sheila-san, was it?

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.340
Y-Yes.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.600
Tell him how you feel.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:17.470
Huh?

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.600
Women are meant to love at any time.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:27.110
However, the old man is a bit much, though.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:29.400
Seriously, the old man is a bit much.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.830
Totally not happening.

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:37.000
I wonder if she's considered positive boobs.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:37.770
Eh?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.340
20 Days Until They Land On Mars

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.320
O...

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:06.130
Ow!

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:11.390
See? That's the only thing he's good at.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.550
The only thing ever since we were kids...

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.120
Yeah... That's the only thing... 
I wouldn't stand a chance.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:21.670
Stop saying that's the only thing!

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:24.690
Just try and say that one 
more time, you bastard!

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.700
That blonde guy's in the same 
squad as you guys, right?

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.200
Man, he's super pissed.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.630
Shouldn't we stop him?

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:36.480
Um... exactly what part didn't you like?

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.860
The part where I said,

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:42.610
"your parents sold you and your 
brother for less than your house"?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:47.630
Or was it "because your mom 
couldn't sell herself anymore"?

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:51.520
Or "thank goodness your brother was able 
to die peacefully during the surgery"?

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.280
You bastard!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:53.860
Hold...

00:09:58.780 --> 00:09:59.540
...on.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:02.660
Why you...

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.660
Stop.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:08.490
So you couldn't handle the pressure 
of the mission, and started a fight.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:15.130
Most of you will die during
 the mission without trying.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.180
Vermin should just act like vermin.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:35.840
I'm sorry our teammate hurt you so much.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.500
I apologize... I just got really pissed off.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.650
Everyone's so on edge right now.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.260
Anyway, thank you.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.680
Um... You're from Russia, right?

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.550
Ah, I'm Ivan.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:53.920
No worries! I'm always like this.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:58.440
My sister always calls me an idiot.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.320
But it's not something that 
just anyone can do...

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.960
You must have a lot of courage.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.260
You're so obvious!

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.780
Love at first sight...

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:23.240
But, Ivan, if you fall in love with 
Sheila, it'll be a tough battle.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.240
Considering the one 
Sheila likes is the Captain.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:37.690
Uh, um... let's keep that off the records...

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:38.700
It's too late for that!

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.880
How did you know that?!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.670
Er, well, I thought I heard 
Michelle-san mention it before...

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.100
Come to think of it, how did she know...

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.100
H-Hey, get a hold of yourself.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.600
I'm fine.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.750
I'm more of a man than he is.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.900
Wanna play catch?

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:00.540
Yeah.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:36.020
Azara City
Saitama Prefecture

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.780
Just 3 More Hours

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.780
Until Landing On Mars

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.520
Welcome.

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.880
I'll have Maou Gaisen on the rocks.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.550
Coming right up.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.550
To think I'd find you in Japan.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:14.560
Despite all that's happened, 
we're heading back to Mars once again.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.190
I'm sure that was a surprise to you 
when you heard it on the news.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.200
What might you be talking about, sir?

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:31.470
I am the Deputy Commander of 
U-NASA's Annex 1 project

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:35.080
and Major of the Japanese air 
and self defense force,

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:38.210
Hiruma Shichisei.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.210
Professor Honda...

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:44.470
Correct?

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.220
Twenty years ago, on the Bugs 2 project...

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.290
You were involved with that 
project as an engineer,

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:03.230
and tried to surpass the other signatories 
as well as Komachi-san, but failed.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:07.610
By using my older brother, Hiruma Ichiro.

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:12.870
I'm surprised you were 
able to live this long.

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:19.000
Actually... I'm thankful that you're alive.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:24.870
I didn't come here as an 
employee of U-NASA today.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.820
As I introduced myself earlier,

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:31.010
I'm someone who protects Japan.

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.160
I need your help, and your information.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.240
Let's talk about things in order.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
About the Annex project,

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.410
which is different from the Bugs project.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:53.780
Here.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.650
Here I go!

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:00.460
<i>All personnel,</i>

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.550
<i>this is your captain speaking.</i>

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:07.170
<i>It has been thirty-nine days 
since we left the Earth.</i>

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:11.320
<i>Our vessel is heading to 
Mars smoothly, and will be</i>

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.470
<i>entering its atmosphere momentarily.</i>

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:17.430
<i>All personnel should gather 
in Area A in two hours.</i>

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.230
<i>Once we have confirmed all of our equipment, 
in accordance with Plan Alpha,</i>

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.610
we will begin our mission to land on Mars.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.760
Are you sure, Sheila-chan?

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.240
You even learned Japanese from Akari-kun...

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:36.410
Yeah...

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:45.010
<i>I'm trying to act like I'm helping 
Sheila-chan, but in reality,</i>

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.260
<i>I'm just trying not to think about my fear.</i>

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:51.790
<i>But it's probably not just me...</i>

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:56.600
<i>I mean, once we're on Mars...</i>

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.470
Are you scared, Eva?

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:08.030
No matter how scared you are,

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:11.240
it is important that you 
learn about what you fear.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:17.060
If humans are born with

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.330
only one weapon, 
it is the ability to feel fear,

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:24.460
accept it, cope with it, 
and set up some plan

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:28.960
not only when we're about to 
die, but far prior to that.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:33.860
We officers know how to defeat those things.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:37.770
It'll be all right, Eva.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.680
You have ninety-nine others at your side.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:44.720
Even if you are fearful,

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:47.440
the hundred of us will cope with it.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.320
<i>Even then... no...</i>

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:58.280
<i>I wish we would never make it to Mars.</i>

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:02.160
<i>Michelle, are you able to move right now?</i>

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.090
Hm?

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:04.400
<i>Numerous security cameras</i>

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:06.740
in Area D and Area S aren't functioning.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:08.670
Could you go check on those for me?

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:15.680
Who could still be in the shower?

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.300
One of the Chinese girls 
was in there earlier.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:20.310
She's taking a pretty long shower.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:24.330
Well... I wonder why we smell 
this particular scent.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:29.260
It's not exactly shampoo... 
but the scent of a woman.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:31.290
Indeed.

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:38.210
And is it wrong as an organism, 
to be drawn by such a scent?

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:40.580
I don't believe that it is, Sensei!

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:49.990
Er... Um, I was just...

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.550
I was worried you might 
have passed out, so...

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.420
I-I'm so sorry!

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:10.550
Those things are able to get in anywhere.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.140
Wh-Why...

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.920
We're not even on Mars yet!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:28.600
<i>It's a miracle...</i>

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:32.030
<i>It's a miracle I was able to dodge that.</i>

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:36.490
<i>It's just like when a cockroach evades 
the human's first blow.</i>

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.800
<i>It doesn't change our obvious and 
absolute difference in strength.</i>

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:41.880
Marcos...

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.340
I'll keep dodging. You run to the storehouse!

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:47.940
Wh-What are you...?

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:51.110
If we both run and it comes after 
us, we're both going to die!

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.070
Go!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.410
Well, come at me!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:08.190
Michelle-san...

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.960
Go after Marcos.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:12.180
No, I'm going to fight, too!

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:14.730
Everyone who's undergone the surgery

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.590
needs the medicine to activate their powers,

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.020
but none of us have that right now.

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:21.590
Without the medication, the ones with the

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.450
most energy are just you 
and me, Michelle-san!

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.970
That's exactly why.

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:31.060
If there happens to be more 
than one, Marcos is in danger

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:32.680
You need to protect him.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.090
I-It can't be...

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.690
Where did they get in?!

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:09.740
Wh-Where's the medicine?!

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:10.980
In the storehouse!

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.370
Everyone get back!

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:14.610
Th-That's...

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:17.470
Yeah, it's just for crowd control.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:21.740
It's just used for thieves! 
But I don't have a choice!

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:27.420
Someone hurry up and get 
to the storehouse now!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.790
<i>The medicine...</i>

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.880
If you happen to get into a close 
quarters battle with a terraformar,

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:37.420
use the medicine.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.570
The use of the medicine puts 
a lot of stress on the body,

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:45.990
but it'll bring out the abilities you've 
received from your surgery.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.840
<i>If only I had that medicine...</i>

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.130
O-Oh God...

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:34.440
We're opening it.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.540
Washington, this is Annex 1.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:21:59.460
This plan...

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.110
...has failed!

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:41.490
<b><i>To the Planet of Calamity</i></b>
